> A while ago Ray Chason suggested Unicode Nethack [1] so that we code
> use different accents to distinguish different kinds of monsters, while
> retaining the classic text-mode feel. I don't know whether he got
> anywhere with implementing it though. It shouldn't be too hard to
> implement, I imagine, if you have a terminal that supports unicode.
This occasionally come up on rec.games.roguelike.development as well. 
Another idea that appears with it is the use of appropriate character 
sets for non-western-european monsters.  For example, a Japanese symbol 
for Tengu, runes for Viking monsters, and evil-looking scripts for 
demons.  Of course, the symbols offer a fair amount of possibilities as 
well.
With all canines as d and all dragons as D, it might be a good idea to 
use every d-sound letter in the basic multilingual plane to try and 
distinguish them more.
